
		       GNU Zebra alpha version
				   
			  Kunihiro Ishiguro

			       May 1998

1. Introduction

GNU Zebra is a free software that manages TCP/IP based routing
protocol.  It takes multi-server and multi-thread approach to resolve
the current complexity of the Internet. Zebra supports RIPv1, RIPv2
and BGP-4 and will support OSPFv2.  Zebra works as Route Server and
Route Reflector. IPv6 is also supported, so zebra can speak BGP4+ and
RIPng.


2. GNU Zebra web page and how to get Zebra

WWW page is located at:

  http://www.zebra.org/

And alpha version source file can be found at:

  ftp://ftp.zebra.org/pub/zebra/

Currently GNU Zebra is under rapidly development, so I recommend you
to get the latest version of zebra.


3. Supported plat-home

Now GNU Zebra is testing on 

  o FreeBSD 2.2.5
      -- without IPv6 ;-)
      -- with INRIA IPv6
      -- with Hydrangea
  o GNU/Linux 2.0.33

I'm planning to support

  o GNU/Hurd 0.2
  o Solaris 2.6


4. Install

You will need GNU C Compiler (aka gcc).  Please see `INSTALL' file.
Basically

  % configure
  % make

will make all daemons.

  # make install

will install 'zebra' and 'bgpd' and 'ripd' under $prefix/sbin/.


5. Configuration

Each daemon's configuration file is called '*.conf'.  If you want to
use vty interface (terminal interface of each daemon), you must
configure terminal password.

 o Sample configuration
 
  !
  ! zebra configuration sample
  !
  hostname Router
  password zebra
  !

Next run daemon, and connect from each daemon's vty port will show like below.

  % telnet localhost 2601
  Trying 127.0.0.1...
  Connected to localhost.
  Escape character is '^]'.

  Hello, this is zebra (version alpha-01)
  Copyright 1997 Kunihiro Ishiguro


  User Access Verification

  Password: XXXXX
  Router> help 
          ~~~~
will show you the command list of zebra.


6. Daemons

6.1 zebra

  zebra [OPTIONS...]
    -d, --daemon       Runs in daemon mode.
    -f, --config_file  Set configuration file name. Default is 'zebra.conf'
    -P, --vty_port     Set vty's port number (default is 2602).
    -v, --version      Print program version.
    -h, --help         Display help and exit.

6.2 ripd

  ripd [OPTIONS...]
    -d, --daemon       Runs in daemon mode.
    -f, --config_file  Set configuration file name.
    -P, --vty_port     Set vty's port number (default is 2602).
    -v, --version      Print program version.
    -h, --help         Display help and exit.

6.3 bgpd

  bgpd [-d] [-p port] [-P port] [-f filename] [-v]
    -d            run bgpd as daemon program.
    -p port       set BGP server port number as port.
    -P port       set vty port to port.  Default is 2603.
    -f filename   specify config filename. default is 'zebra.conf'.
    -v            display version information.

7. Ports

Each daemon has each own terminal interface.  Also zebra has
communication port which provides several services to other daemons.
Below is zebra ports list.

zebrasrv      2600/tcp		  # zebra service
zebra	      2601/tcp		  # zebra vty
ripd	      2602/tcp		  # RIPd vty
ripngd	      2603/tcp		  # RIPngd vty
ospfd	      2604/tcp		  # OSPFd vty
bgpd	      2605/tcp		  # BGPd vty

I recommend you to add upper list to /etc/services.


8. automake

GNU Zebra's Makefile.in is generated by `automake' packages.  If you
want to remake Makefile.in please invoke below command at top
directory.

automake --gnu --include-deps
